  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is driven by three primary failure modes: premature breakeven triggers (Trade 4 exited with +3.32 gross P&L via STOP_LOSS at 0.9R, turning into a net loss after \u20b94.04 in fees), afternoon time-decay stagnations (Trades 6 and 10 entered post-13:45 and bled out to EOD_SQUARE_OFF), and tight 0.60% stop-loss whipsaws on high-beta metals like TATASTEEL (Trades 2 and 5). Furthermore, four of the seven losses clustered on a single choppy session (2026-10-22), where static 2.4x volume multipliers failed to filter out range-bound retail noise.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a \u20b910,000 capital base, statutory transaction costs (~0.15% round-trip) severely penalize premature breakeven stops and low-momentum afternoon entries; profitability requires wider structural stops (0.70%+) to survive intraday liquidity sweeps, paired with higher volume conviction (2.7x) and larger targets (1.35%) to overcome fee drag.",
    "parameter_patch": {
