      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.7
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #54 Quantitative Forensics & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash achieved net profitability (\u20b9+3.54, PF 1.04), outperforming the 1-year baseline (PF 0.83), but suffered from severe fee drag (\u20b944.35 fees across 12 trades) and a 27.05% max drawdown. Forensic analysis of the 7 losing trades revealed that a `0.60%` stop-loss is repeatedly hunted by routine intraday noise in high-beta counters like TATASTEEL, while a `0.9R` breakeven trigger chokes winning trades (e.g., ICICIBANK) into net fee losses before trend expansion occurs. To harden the strategy for Cycle #55, we are widening `min_sl_pct` to `0.70%` to absorb NSE microstructure whipsaws, elevating `breakeven_trigger_r` to `1.25R` to ensure trades clear statutory brokerage/STT hurdles before locking stops, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `2.70x` to eliminate choppy mid-day/afternoon false breakouts, and expanding `min_target_pct` to `1.35%` to skew asymmetric reward-to-risk post-fees."
